{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_invvcnx6drxe2h7quuv5ykq5fh7a5pihp6x7x3tljusyonwcj7uq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — driver exits 0, zero failure markers.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 19-line function, `void flip_horizontal(cp_image_t *img)`, which — despite its name — swaps whole **rows** (a vertical flip). That discrepancy is preserved, not \"fixed\".\n\n## Phase A artifacts (all mechanically derived)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly one non-toolchain symbol, `flip_horizontal`; the Rust `.so` exports it too. Symbol diff empty, 0 undefined non-libc symbols, verified for **both** profiles. No C module was left untranslated (CMake compiles one file).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 19 rows. Greps prove the library has *no* error mechanism at all: no `return`, no `assert`, no null check, no range check, no enum. So every rejection is either a silent no-op (a loop guard false on entry) or a hardware fault, and I defined \"same rejection\" accordingly.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 32 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (only two `for` guards exist), plus the one case I could *not* test and why.\n\n## Two real fidelity bugs found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **`img == NULL`: C → SIGSEGV(11), Rust → SIGABRT(6).** rustc instruments *place-expression* derefs (`(*img).pix`) with a null check under `-C debug-assertions`; the panic can't unwind out of `extern \"C\"`, so it aborts. I isolated this with a standalone rustc experiment comparing four deref primitives, then switched the three header loads to `core::ptr::read(&raw const …)`. This is also why the `pix == NULL` row passed from the start — the pixel loads already used `.read()`.\n2. **`offset`/`add` → `wrapping_offset`/`wrapping_add`.** Those carry a checked \"must not wrap the address space\" precondition that aborts on the large-negative-`w` inputs C accepts silently (the inner loop never runs, so the pointer is computed and discarded).\n\n## A trap worth flagging\n\n`cargo test` does **not** build a `cdylib`, because the tests `dlopen` rather than link it. My first \"27 passed\" run was silently validating a *stale* `.so` from before my edits. I added an `assert_so_fresh` mtime guard (confirmed it fires) and a driver that builds both profiles first — otherwise this suite could pass against dead code indefinitely.\n\n## Harness self-validation\n\nPassing tests prove little on their own, so I injected four bugs; **all four detected**. Notably mutant A (`flips = (h+1)/2`) is *semantically equivalent* for every finite `h` — the extra iteration self-swaps — and was caught only because it dereferences a NULL `pix` when `h == 1`.\n\n## One documented gap\n\nSigned overflow of `w * i` **while the result is dereferenced** is untestable: overflow needs `w*h > 2^31` pixels, and dereferencing needs that memory resident — ~8 GB. The overflow arithmetic is covered on non-dereferencing shapes; `wrapping_mul` matches gcc at the `-O0` CMake uses. I recorded this in `CONFIGS.md` rather than checking the row off silently.\n\nOnly one feature configuration exists (no `[features]` table — confirmed by parsing `Cargo.toml`), verified under both `dev` and `release`. `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":114908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":280,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6b563dc-7211-46b6-8fa6-c3286c140108","uuid":"17702134-5334-48b6-9bec-8620e632d67c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:21:22.280Z"}
